    "world_valid": "all five non-learning baselines fail AND the weak teacher-first baseline fails AND the independent reference solver returns a complete action sequence that replays to feasible without early termination",
    "world_invalid": "at least one of the six baselines is feasible (the world is too easy)",
    "world_unknown": "all six baselines fail but no reference witness exists (bounded program search); unknown is discarded and is never reported as unsolvable",
    "reference": "tactical_teacher_validation.solve (independent bounded program class, no teacher geometry consulted) plus an explicit non-early verify() replay of every witness",
    "discard": "mirror pairs share one group and one split; a group is retained only if base and mirror both come out valid; duplicates of any frozen signature are discarded before evaluation",
    "no_relaxation": "if a family cannot reach six valid groups inside its budget the actual number and the per-candidate reasons are reported; no threshold is loosened",
